Stable Bible Assistant Bot
A robust, production-ready Telegram bot that leverages Large Language Models (LLMs) and specialized scripture libraries to provide a seamless Bible study experience.

  Overview
This project integrates the Llama-3.3-70b model (via Groq) with the pythonbible library to create an intelligent assistant capable of providing context-aware biblical insights and instant KJV scripture retrieval.

  Key Features
Dual-Logic Processing: Automatically detects scripture references (e.g., "John 3:16") for direct retrieval or falls back to AI chat for theological questions.

Sliding Window Memory: Implements a conversation buffer that retains the last 12 messages, ensuring the bot stays focused without exceeding token limits.

HTML Rich Formatting: Delivers beautifully formatted responses using Telegram’s HTML parse mode for bold headers and italicized verses.

Production Security: Fully decoupled configuration using environment variables to protect sensitive API credentials.

Asynchronous Architecture: Built on python-telegram-bot's asyncio framework for high-concurrency performance.

  Tech Stack
Language: Python 3.10+

APIs: Groq Cloud (Llama 3.3), Telegram Bot API

Libraries: pythonbible, python-dotenv, python-telegram-bot

Deployment: Optimized for Linux VPS (Ubuntu) with Systemd process management.

  Setup & Installation
Clone the repository:

Bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/telegram-bible-bot.git
cd telegram-bible-bot
Install dependencies:

Bash
   pip install -r requirements.txt
Configure Environment Variables:
Create a .env file in the root directory and add your keys:

Plaintext
   GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_key_here
   TELEGRAM_TOKEN=your_telegram_token_here
Run the bot:

Bash
python bot_logic.py
